== Trivia ==
* They are randomly encountered as an alternate version of {{e|Pride}}.
** Despite this, Edmund's attacks mirror {{e|Super Sloth}}'s more than Pride's.
*** This is supported by both Edmund and Super Sloth having the same entity ID of 46.
* Ultra Pride may be a reference to the book Frankenstein, in which Victor Frankenstein creates a living being he deems a monster. The creation of life is often considered the ultimate act of pride. In this case, Florian takes the place of Frankenstein and Edmund takes the place of the monster.
** It might also be a reference to the fact that inserting yourself into your own video-game is often seen as narcissistic.
** Ultra Pride's first appearance was in the final update to the flash version of ''The Binding of Isaac'' and was believed by fans to symbolize Edmund's "Ultimate Pride" at both the success of, and the fact he had finally finished development on ''The Binding of Isaac''.
* Florian Himsl was the programmer of the first [[wikipedia:The Binding of Isaac (video game)|''The Binding of Isaac'']] game.
* Ultra Pride (Edmund) is one of five enemies (four without Repentance, three without Afterbirth+) in the game that uses [[Creep]] as projectiles, the others are {{e|Conjoined Fatty}}, {{e|Bloaty}}, {{e|Meatball}}, and {{e|The Thing}}.
* The [[wikipedia:Seven Deadly Sins|Seven Deadly Sins]] that these mini-bosses are based upon are, in Christian teachings, a classification of vices from which all others are derived from.
* {{dlc+|r}} Florian dropping the {{i|Eternal D6}} is a reference to the Eternal Edition of the original game, which was a free update developed by Florian.
* According to Edmund in a [https://twitter.com/edmundmcmillen/status/1733332795353923624?s=20 twitter AMA], the other deadly sins were supposed to have ultra forms as well, however they were scrapped for unknown reasons.{{dlc-}}
* Edmund dropping/unlocking the Left Hand trinket may be a reference to how Edmund is left handed in real life.
